/// Files a program asks a host to write.
///
///    Nothing here reaches a filesystem. `write` puts a (path, text)
/// pair into the agent's `output_files`, and what becomes of it is the host's
/// business: the CLI drains that map in `post_eval` and turns each symbol
/// into a filename, and a browser has no equivalent yet -- which is why a
/// scene written this way cannot be read back there (#69).
///
/// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
module {

    /// Ask the host to write `text` under the name `path`.
    ///
    /// The path is a symbol rather than a text, and the CLI renders it with
    /// the backticks removed -- so `` `demand-`size-`dat `` becomes the file
    /// `demand-size-dat`.
    public func write(path : Symbol, text : Text) {
        prim "writeFile" (path, text)
    };

}
